## Interface: 11509, 20506, 16001
## Title: Readycheck |cff33ff99Reminders|r
## Notes: The reminder stack: the trigger engine that decides when to warn you, the popup itself, kill-time modelling and the raid route.
## Author: Zac
## Version: 1.0
## Dependencies: Readycheck
## LoadOnDemand: 1
## IconTexture: Interface\Icons\INV_Misc_Bell_01

# Four layers that all answer "tell the player to do something now", kept
# in one addon so they switch off as a unit:
#   Core_Reminders   the popup frame, its icons, animation and dismissal
#   Trigger          evaluates each boss's ability config and raises them
#   TTK              kill-time model and execute-phase prediction
#   Route            the ordered raid route and its use-watching
#
# TTK and Route are not reminders, but both feed the trigger engine
# (ttk triggers read PredictTTK, route steps raise reminders) and neither
# stands up without it, so splitting them further just moved the seam.
#
# ALL SETTINGS STAY IN ReadycheckDB, plus executeSettings for the TTK
# history. They belong to the main addon on purpose: switching this off
# must not throw a single setting away, and switching it back on has to
# pick up exactly where it left off.
#
# What the main addon keeps, and why it survives this addon being off:
#   Core\Core_Stubs.lua        no-op fallback for every method below that
#                              core calls unguarded - see that file first
#   Core\Core_Boot.lua         CreateFontString, FormatTime
#   Systems\RaidData\RaidLookup.lua
#                              boss/add/trash name resolution, which the
#                              gear stack calls on every boss death
#   Systems\Trigger\TE_Events  the single event pump, shared with gear
#   Systems\TTSEngine.lua      the speech engine the reminders talk through
#   Core_Events                SmartDismissReminder and friends
#   UI\Sidebar\Sidebar_PagesStatsBar.lua
#                              stats bar and buff pushoff pages, which
#                              used to share a file with the reminder page

# ---------- The popup ----------
# Defines RC:ShowReminder and the frame everything below draws into, so
# nothing here moves above it.
Core_Reminders.lua

# ---------- Kill-time model ----------
# Model defines RC.executeCalculator and its defaults; History and Execute
# both read that table at load, so Model stays first.
TTK\TTK_Model.lua
TTK\TTK_History.lua
TTK\TTK_Execute.lua

# ---------- Trigger engine ----------
# Reads RC._tes, the reuse tables built in the main addon's
# Systems\Trigger\TE_GearSwap.lua - already loaded by the time we get here.
# Triggers must precede Encounters: the encounter gates call back into it.
Trigger\TE_Triggers.lua
Trigger\TE_Encounters.lua
Trigger\TE_Reminders.lua

# ---------- TTK display ----------
# Draws from the model above and is registered with UIMover, so it loads
# after both are in place.
TTK\TTKDisplay.lua

# ---------- Individual reminders ----------
Reminders\EquipmentReminder.lua
Reminders\BattleShoutReminder.lua
Reminders\BoonReminder.lua
Reminders\CustomReminders.lua
# Raid buff and boss debuff trackers: one engine, two instances.
Reminders\AuraTracker.lua

# ---------- Raid route ----------
# Engine defines RC.RaidRoute and the store; Tracker and UseWatch drive it.
Route\RR_Engine.lua
Route\RR_Tracker.lua
Route\RR_UseWatch.lua

# ---------- UI, last ----------
# These register sidebar pages and read every table built above. The
# Cons_* pages read RC._sbc, published by the main addon's
# UI\Consumables\Cons_Base.lua, which stays there because the consumables
# and boss-notes pages share it.
# The kit first: row builders the pages below share (RC._rpk).
UI\Reminders_PageKit.lua
UI\Sidebar_PagesReminders.lua
UI\Sidebar_PagesExecute.lua
UI\SidebarCustomReminders.lua
UI\Cons_BattleShout.lua
UI\Cons_Boon.lua
UI\Cons_AuraTracker.lua
UI\Route\Route_Helpers.lua
UI\Route\Route_Render.lua
# The From Logs window: the route page's link, Copy my character, Paste Route
UI\Route\Route_FromLogs.lua
